      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The suburb’s fresh‑water spring, fed by Table Mountain, powered the historic Josephine Mill and early brewing in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        12,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newlands%2C_Cape_Town",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Newlands Brewery, founded in 1820, still brews Castle Lager and sits beside the rugby grounds that host Newlands Stadium.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/south-africa/western-cape_newlands",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Liesbeek River runs through Newlands, passing the Vineyard Hotel and once supplied the first European‑style beer in southern Africa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newlands%2C_Cape_Town",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Newlands Cricket Ground, established in the 19th century, remains a premier international venue surrounded by leafy streets and historic homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
